Group 3: file open/close and block I/O

test 300: 1 s/b 1 (fopen for write)
test 301: 0 s/b 0 (fclose)
test 302: "line one
" s/b "line one
"
test 303: "value=42
" s/b "value=42
"
test 304: X s/b X (fgetc)
test 305: -1 s/b -1 (EOF at end)
test 306: 1 s/b 1 (feof set)
test 307: "line" "one" s/b "line" "one"
test 308: i=42 s/b 42
test 310: 8 s/b 8 (fwrite count)
test 311: 8 "ABCDEFGH" s/b 8 "ABCDEFGH"
test 312: 2 "ABCDEFGH" s/b 2 "ABCDEFGH"
test 313: 0 s/b 0 (rename succeeds)
test 314: 1 s/b 1 (old name gone)
test 315: "moved" s/b "moved"
test 316: 0 s/b 0 (rename replaces target)
test 317: "fresh" s/b "fresh"
test 318: 1 s/b 1 (rename of missing file fails)

Group 4: file positioning

test 400: 5 s/b 5 (ftell after seek)
test 401: 5 s/b 5 (char at offset 5)
test 402: 8 s/b 8 (char after relative seek)
test 403: 7 s/b 7 (char from end seek)
test 404: 0 s/b 0 (ftell after rewind)
test 405: 4 s/b 4 (char after fsetpos)

Group 5: character I/O, pushback, status and misc

test 500: 0 0 s/b 0 0 (ungetc replays char)
test 501: Z s/b Z (ungetc arbitrary)
test 502: Q s/b Q (putc/getc)
test 503: 1 s/b 1 (feof before clear)
test 504: 0 s/b 0 (feof after clearerr)
test 505: 0 s/b 0 (ferror clean)
test 506: 1 s/b 1 (fileno of stdout)
test 507: "alpha" s/b "alpha"
test 508: 0 s/b 0 (remove)
test 509: 1 s/b 1 (file gone after remove)

Group 6: buffering

test 600: 0 s/b 0 (full buffered, nothing on disk yet)
test 601: 5 "hello" s/b 5 "hello" (visible after flush)
test 602: 3 "bye" s/b 3 "bye" (fclose flushed)
test 603: 3 "now" s/b 3 "now" (unbuffered, immediate)
test 604: 0 s/b 0 (line buffered, no newline yet)
test 605: 4 "abc
" s/b 4 "abc\n" (flushed at newline)
test 606: 0 s/b 0 (setvbuf user buffer)
test 607: "user buffered data" s/b "user buffered data"
test 608: 2000 s/b 2000 (large fwrite count)
test 609: 2000 s/b 2000 (large fread count)
test 610: 3 s/b 3 (read after buffered write)
test 611: X s/b X (write after read)

Group 7: temporary files

test 700: "/tmp/tmp.*.1" "/tmp/tmp.*.2" distinct=1 s/b 1
test 701: 1 s/b 1 (name does not pre-exist)
test 702: 1 s/b 1 (length 18 < L_tmpnam 64)
test 703: 1 s/b 1 (tmpnam(NULL) returns a name)
test 704: 1 s/b 1 (tmpfile opens)
test 705: "scratch data" s/b "scratch data"

Group 8: direct FILE access (backdoor accessors)

test 800: 0 s/b 0 (fpending after flush)
test 801: 3 s/b 3 (fpending tracks pending writes)
test 802: 1 s/b 1 (fwritable on wb+)
test 803: 18 s/b >0 (freadahead reports read ahead)
test 804: 18 s/b 18 (freadahead == bytes actually buffered)
test 805: 1 s/b 1 (ferror sees a directly set error)
test 806: 4 s/b 4 (_fileno matches fileno())
test 807: 0 s/b 0 (fwritable on rb)
test 808: 1 s/b 1 (freadable on rb)

All self checking tests passed.
